      "writtenOn": "2025-11-11T15:15:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I imagine we could address this a different way: instead of having this PKVM_FIRST_INOUT_PV_INTERFACE as a \"delimiter\", use a separate macro `PKVM_HC_INOUT()` for those interfaces that should use inout, and add something like this to (kvm_)pkvm.h:\n\n```\nstatic inline bool pkvm_fn_use_inout(enum pkvm_fn fn)\n{\n\tswitch (fn) {\n\t#define PKVM_HC(fn)\n\t#define PKVM_HC_INOUT(fn)\tcase fn:\n\t#include \u003casm/kvm_pkvm_hypercalls.h\u003e\n\t\treturn true;\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n...BTW maybe also worth renaming `pkvm_fn` to `pkvm_hc`?",
      "parentUuid": "b7362be8_9ef5a65f",
      "revId": "19e533e94040afc2959502b4b8b28d10ab6705dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
